---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import InquiryForm from "../components/InquiryForm.astro";
---
<Base
  wide
  title="Work with me"
  description="Private quantitative coaching, research-methods guidance, and institutional econometrics training with Dr. Ian Helfrich. See fit, formats, and starting rates."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Private practice · Institutional training</span>
    <h1>Serious help for quantitative work.</h1>
    <p class="kicker">
      Bring the course, model, dataset, paper, or methods problem that is keeping you stuck. We will turn it into a sequence you can reason through—and ultimately own.
    </p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button" href="#formats">See formats and rates</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="#inquiry">Start an inquiry</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section compact" aria-labelledby="fit-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">Fit comes first</span>
        <h2 id="fit-title">I am useful when understanding is the constraint.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>I will say so directly if your problem needs a different specialist, a lawyer, an accountant, a full-service analyst, or simply more time than I can responsibly offer.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="fit-list">
      <div>
        <h3>Strong fit</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>You want to understand the method, not merely obtain an answer.</li>
          <li>The work involves econometrics, statistics, economics, finance, research design, or quantitative software.</li>
          <li>You are willing to show your reasoning and revise it.</li>
          <li>You value candor, preparation, and methodological care.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Not a fit</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>You want graded work, an exam, or a paper completed for you.</li>
          <li>You need guaranteed grades, publication, or statistical significance.</li>
          <li>You are seeking uncredited authorship or undisclosed analysis.</li>
          <li>The engagement would violate your institution's rules.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="formats" class="section" aria-labelledby="formats-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">New independent engagements</span>
        <h2 id="formats-title">Choose the smallest format that can solve the problem.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>These are starting points, not mystery pricing. Scope, preparation, urgency, and institutional requirements can change a quote; you will know the price before work begins.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="pricing-grid">
      <article class="price-card">
        <span class="card-tag">Focused</span>
        <h3>Private session</h3>
        <span class="price">$225 <small>/ 60 minutes</small></span>
        <p>For a defined concept, problem set of your own work, code issue, model, or decision.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Brief pre-session intake</li>
          <li>Live one-to-one instruction</li>
          <li>Session notes when useful</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="price-card featured">
        <span class="card-tag">Diagnose</span>
        <h3>Methods diagnostic</h3>
        <span class="price">$325 <small>/ 75 minutes</small></span>
        <p>For a paper, thesis, dissertation, or applied project that needs a defensible path forward.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Materials reviewed in advance</li>
          <li>Research-design working session</li>
          <li>Concise written roadmap</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="price-card">
        <span class="card-tag">Accelerate</span>
        <h3>Four-week intensive</h3>
        <span class="price">From $1,800</span>
        <p>For a compressed runway: difficult course unit, qualifying exam, replication, or research milestone.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Six structured sessions</li>
          <li>Custom practice and resources</li>
          <li>Between-session continuity</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="fine-print">
      Rates above apply to new clients who find me independently. Existing arrangements remain governed by their current agreements. If you first contacted me through Wyzant, scheduling and payment remain on Wyzant under the platform's rules.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="subjects-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">Subject range</span>
        <h2 id="subjects-title">Deep methods. Broad economic context.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>My comparative advantage is connecting mathematical intuition, research design, software, and economic interpretation.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="method-grid">
      <article class="method-card">
        <h3>Econometrics & statistics</h3>
        <p>Regression, panel data, DiD, RDD, IV, synthetic control, event studies, inference, probability, experimental design, and model diagnostics.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="method-card">
        <h3>Economics & finance</h3>
        <p>Microeconomics, macroeconomics, international trade, networks, public policy, corporate finance, capital markets, and economic reasoning.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="method-card">
        <h3>Research workflows</h3>
        <p>R, Stata, Python, Excel, Julia, LaTeX, replication, data cleaning, visualization, spatial analysis, code review, and research communication.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="institutions" class="ethics-panel" aria-labelledby="institution-title">
    <div>
      <span class="section-label">Departments, labs, and teams</span>
      <h2 id="institution-title">Custom training that survives the workshop.</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>Institutional engagements combine live instruction with reusable materials, worked examples, and a scope matched to the team's actual data and decisions.</p>
      <p><strong>Half-day workshops begin at $5,000.</strong> Cohorts, full-day programs, custom curriculum, and ongoing office hours are scoped separately.</p>
      <p><a class="button small" href="#inquiry">Request an institutional scope</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section compact" aria-labelledby="process-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">Process</span>
        <h2 id="process-title">Simple, written, and clear.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>No pressure call and no vague sales funnel. We establish fit, scope, price, boundaries, and scheduling before paid work begins.</p>
    </div>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Send a short inquiry.</strong> Describe the work, your timeline, and where you are stuck.</li>
      <li><strong>I assess fit.</strong> I reply with the right format, a clarifying question, a referral, or an honest no.</li>
      <li><strong>We confirm the engagement.</strong> Scope, rate, preparation, scheduling, cancellation terms, and academic-integrity boundaries are written down.</li>
      <li><strong>We do the work together.</strong> Every session is oriented toward independent command, not ongoing dependence.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="section compact" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">Common questions</span>
        <h2 id="faq-title">Before you ask.</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <details>
      <summary>Do you offer reduced student rates?</summary>
      <p>A small number of reduced-rate places may be available when capacity allows. Tell me honestly in the inquiry. I do not promise availability, and urgent work is not discounted.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Will you work directly in my code or data?</summary>
      <p>Often, yes—alongside you and within an instructional or advisory scope. I can demonstrate, review, debug, and explain. I will not quietly become the undisclosed analyst or author of work represented as solely yours.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can you guarantee a grade, result, or publication?</summary>
      <p>No. I can improve the quality of your reasoning, preparation, and execution. Outcomes still depend on your work, your institution, your data, and factors neither of us controls.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do you meet remotely?</summary>
      <p>Yes. Most private and institutional work is remote, with timezone-aware scheduling. In-person Atlanta engagements can be discussed when the format warrants it.</p>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section id="inquiry" class="section" aria-labelledby="inquiry-title">
    <div class="inquiry-layout">
      <aside class="inquiry-aside">
        <span class="section-label">Start here</span>
        <h2 id="inquiry-title">Tell me what is at stake.</h2>
        <p>The useful details are:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>what you are working on,</li>
          <li>what you have tried,</li>
          <li>where the reasoning breaks down, and</li>
          <li>the real timeline.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>I typically answer serious inquiries within two business days.</strong></p>
      </aside>
      <InquiryForm />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
